adversarial-review fixes (self-audit of the whole build)

Found and fixed 3 real defects, each with a regression test that now stays enforced:

1. Web UI broke once a token was set: the browser never sent the bearer token, so
   switch/effort/hermes-sync from the UI returned 403. Fix: the server injects the
   registry token into the served HTML (page only reachable over 127.0.0.1 + Tailscale)
   and the UI's mutating fetches now carry it via X-Launcher-Token. Direct/API callers
   still send their own token. Verified: no-token -> 403, with-token -> 202, token present
   in served page, UI-style hermes-sync -> 200.

2. status() assumed the OpenAI /v1/models shape, so a non-OpenAI engine (Ollama /api/tags)
   was never reported up and never showed its model list. Fix: the health probe now uses the
   engine's registered health_url and parses OpenAI {"data":[{id}]} and Ollama {"models":[{name}]}
   shapes, falling back to the registered api_name. Verified: an Ollama engine reports
   up=True with its model names.

3. journal_since crashed on a None unit/since. Fix: handle None (fall back to the generic tail).

2 new regression tests in test_server.py (test_ui_token_injection_and_auth,
test_status_reports_ollama_up_and_models). 19 tests total, all green.
